<!doctype html>
<html class="no-js" lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="{{ settings.color_background | default: '#070605' }}">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">

  {%- comment -%}
    Falls back to the OPTIQ "O" mark (Bodoni Moda, matching the wordmark
    everywhere else on the site) whenever no favicon has been set in Theme
    Settings - that empty-favicon state is what was showing the browser's
    own default globe icon in the tab.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 48, height: 48 }}">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 180, height: 180 }}">
  {%- else -%}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ images['optiq-favicon-o.png'] | image_url: width: 48, height: 48 }}">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ images['optiq-favicon-o.png'] | image_url: width: 180, height: 180 }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  <title>{{ page_title }}{% unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless %}</title>
  {%- if page_description -%}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} Social sharing metadata {%- endcomment -%}
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ shop.name }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical_url }}">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ page_title | escape }}">
  <meta property="og:type" content="{% if request.page_type == 'product' %}product{% elsif request.page_type == 'article' %}article{% else %}website{% endif %}">
  {%- if page_description -%}
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign og_image = nil
    if request.page_type == 'product' and product.featured_media
      assign og_image = product.featured_media.preview_image
    elsif settings.share_image != blank
      assign og_image = settings.share_image
    endif
  -%}
  {%- if og_image -%}
    <meta property="og:image" content="http:{{ og_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}">
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="{{ 1200 | divided_by: og_image.aspect_ratio | round }}">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Fonts, self-hosted - same three Google Fonts families and weights as
    before (DM Sans 400/500/600, Space Grotesk 500/600/700, Bodoni Moda
    400/500/600/700), just served from this theme's own asset CDN instead
    of fonts.googleapis.com + fonts.gstatic.com. Google serves the exact
    same variable-weight woff2 file for every weight within one family (a
    single file covers its whole weight axis), so this is 3 font files
    total, not 10 - each @font-face below just points a different
    font-weight at the same file, matching how Google's own stylesheet was
    already structured. Same-origin removes a second DNS/TLS handshake and
    the "fetch CSS, discover font URLs, then fetch fonts" waterfall that a
    third-party stylesheet forces - the browser can start these two
    requests the moment it reads this file. Only the two families that
    render above the fold sitewide (DM Sans, the default body font) and on
    the homepage splash specifically (Bodoni Moda, the wordmark) are
    preloaded; Space Grotesk (headings, further down every page) still
    loads, just without jumping the queue.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'dm-sans-variable.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="{{ 'bodoni-moda-variable.woff2' | asset_url }}" crossorigin>
  <style>
    @font-face { font-family: 'DM Sans'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ "dm-sans-variable.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'DM Sans'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 500; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ "dm-sans-variable.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'DM Sans'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ "dm-sans-variable.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'Space Grotesk'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 500; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ "space-grotesk-variable.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'Space Grotesk'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ "space-grotesk-variable.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'Space Grotesk'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ "space-grotesk-variable.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'Bodoni Moda'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ "bodoni-moda-variable.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'Bodoni Moda'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 500; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ "bodoni-moda-variable.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'Bodoni Moda'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ "bodoni-moda-variable.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'Bodoni Moda'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ "bodoni-moda-variable.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
  </style>

  {{ content_for_header }}

  {{ 'optiq-core.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'optiq-components.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'optiq-sections.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  {%- comment -%}
    Retained so templates still running the previous section set keep their
    styling while they are migrated. Safe to remove once every template has
    been rebuilt on the new system.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {{ 'base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'configurator-quote-patch.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  <style>
    :root {
      {%- if settings.color_background != blank %}--o-bg: {{ settings.color_background }};{% endif -%}
      {%- if settings.color_accent != blank %}--o-accent: {{ settings.color_accent }};{% endif -%}
      {%- if settings.color_accent_ink != blank %}--o-accent-ink: {{ settings.color_accent_ink }};{% endif -%}
      {%- if settings.page_width != blank %}--o-max: {{ settings.page_width }}px;{% endif -%}
      --o-logo-h: {{ settings.logo_height | default: 30 }}px;
    }
  </style>

  {%- comment -%}
    Flow-field background: off. The homepage is now the Studio storefront,
    which is a light editorial page - the animated grayscale canvas painted
    a near-black sheet over the whole thing, and its backdrop colour turned
    the body black behind it. Left as a false flag rather than deleted so
    the canvas can be switched back on for a future dark template without
    reconstructing the gate and the matching render below.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign show_flow_bg = false -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Google Review Cards page: plain premium white, same as every other page
    - no marble texture, no dark backdrop.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign show_reviews_bg = false -%}
  {%- if template.suffix == 'reviews' -%}
    {%- assign show_reviews_bg = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if show_reviews_bg -%}
    <style>body.o-flow-page { background: #ffffff; }</style>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    AI Receptionist page: plain premium white too, matching the rest of the
    site - no marble texture, no dark backdrop. The page's own boxes
    (assets/optiq-air.css) are white cards with ink borders now, not black.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign show_air_flow_bg = false -%}
  {%- if template.suffix == 'ai-receptionist' -%}
    {%- assign show_air_flow_bg = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if show_air_flow_bg -%}
    <style>body.o-air-flow { background: #ffffff; }</style>
  {%- endif -%}

  <script>
    // Swap the no-js flag before paint so CSS can rely on it without a flash.
    document.documentElement.classList.remove('no-js');
    window.optiqStrings = {
      cartAdded: {{ 'cart.added' | t | json }},
      cartUpdated: {{ 'cart.updated' | t | json }},
      cartRemoved: {{ 'cart.removed' | t | json }},
      cartError: {{ 'cart.error' | t | json }}
    };
  </script>

  <script src="{{ 'optiq-ui.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
  <script src="{{ 'optiq-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
  <script src="{{ 'optiq-cart.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
</head>

<body class="template-{{ request.page_type | handle }}{% if template == 'index' %} is-home{% endif %}{% if template.suffix == 'reviews' %} o-flow-page{% endif %}{% if show_air_flow_bg %} o-air-flow{% endif %}">
  <a class="o-skip" href="#main-content">{{ 'accessibility.skip_to_content' | t }}</a>

  {%- comment -%}
    Grayscale WebGL flow-field background, carried over from the live theme.
    Same show_flow_bg gate as the background-colour style above, so this
    canvas and its backdrop colour always turn on and off together.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if show_flow_bg -%}
    {% render 'noir-flow-global' %}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="o-live" data-o-live role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></div>

  {% section 'announcement-bar' %}
  {% section 'header' %}

  <main id="main-content" role="main" tabindex="-1">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {% section 'footer' %}

  <div class="o-overlay" data-o-overlay hidden-until-open aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {% section 'cart-drawer' %}

  {%- comment -%}
    Fixed bottom-centre dock. Rendered after the cart drawer so its markup
    sits with the other viewport-anchored UI; stacking is handled by
    z-index in the snippet, not by DOM order.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'optiq-dock' %}

  {%- comment -%}
    Optiq AI storefront assistant. Rendered here so it is present on every
    storefront page. It ships with its own live knowledge payload
    (snippets/optiq-ai-knowledge.liquid), regenerated by Liquid on each page
    load, so the answers always reflect current products, prices, stock and
    pages. Its CSS hides it on the authenticated dashboard and sign-in
    screens, which take over the whole viewport.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'optiq-ai' %}

  {%- comment -%} Organisation schema. Only fields we can state factually. {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
      "url": {{ shop.url | json }}{% if settings.logo %},
      "logo": {{ settings.logo | image_url: width: 512 | prepend: 'https:' | json }}{% endif %}
    }
  </script>

  {%- comment -%}
    WebSite schema, sitewide. The SearchAction points at Shopify's own native
    search route (routes.search_url), which is real, working functionality
    on every page - not a hypothetical or hardcoded path. Built with capture
    rather than a single `{{ }}` expression, since the literal curly braces
    in "{search_term_string}" break Liquid's own tag parser when they sit
    inside a filter chain's string argument.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture search_url_template -%}{{ shop.url }}{{ routes.search_url }}?q={search_term_string}{%- endcapture -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
      "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
      "potentialAction": {
        "@type": "SearchAction",
        "target": {
          "@type": "EntryPoint",
          "urlTemplate": {{ search_url_template | json }}
        },
        "query-input": "required name=search_term_string"
      }
    }
  </script>

</body>
</html>
